Thursday Update
* Trade Alert: Buy Deere calls* Stocks sweep higher as investors applaud be=
tter jobs data--Stocks are rising and the dollar strengthening after initia=
l jobless claims fell to the lowest level since the end of November, beatin=
g market expectations.Through midday, the Dow climbed by 249.33 points, or =
0.8%, to 30,972.11, with S&amp;P 500 higher by 0.8% to 3,859.04 points and =
Nasdaq up by 0.8% to 13,718.24 points. The financials sector was the stando=
ut performer followed by health care and utilities.Initial jobless claims f=
ell to 779,000 during the week ended Jan. 30 from 812,000 a week ago, benea=
th the consensus for 835,000. The four-week moving average dropped to 848,2=
50, breaking the string of recent increases as early January spikes work th=
eir way out of the equation. Continuing claims slid by 193,000 to 4,592,000=
 in the week ended Jan. 23."The third consecutive week of decline, while st=
ill elevated, the ongoing improvement in claims suggests layoffs have slowe=
d, a positive sign for the labor market as well as the broad-based recovery=
 effort," Stifel Chief Economist Lindsey Piegza said in a report. "Steps in=
 the right direction are encouraging that the US economy could and will eve=
ntually return to a stronger jobs position amid a widespread vaccination ef=
fort to contain the virus."Citing data from the Centers for Disease Control=
 and Prevention, UBS said in a research note that vaccination rate has rise=
n in the US and at the current pace the country is on "track to reach herd =
immunity in late June." As per the CDC, the herd immunity threshold for SAR=
S-CoV-2, the virus that causes COVID-19, is expected to range between 50% a=
nd 65%, the note said.Meanwhile, new orders for US factory goods rose by 1.=
1% in December, above expectations for a 0.7% increase in an Econoday surve=
y and following an upwardly revised 1.3% increase in November.In company ne=
ws, shares of Align Technology (ALGN) surged more than 14% intraday, the mo=
st on S&amp;P 500 and Nasdaq, after fourth-quarter sales and earnings beat =
the market expectations. On both the indexes, the steepest decliner was Qua=
lcomm (QCOM), after the company reported fiscal first quarter sales that mi=
ssed guidance, sending shares down by 9% even though earnings beat forecast=
.L Brands (LB) was the second-highest gainer on S&amp;P 500 after the compa=
ny raised earnings guidance for the fourth quarter. The company said Stuart=
 Burgdoerfer is planning to retire as chief financial officer and step down=
 as interim chief executive of Victoria's Secret business. Shares jumped by=
 10%.In the metals markets, silver was down 2.6% to $26.20 an ounce and cop=
per was down 0.5% to $3.55 per pound..Portfolio: We came into today with no=
 positions and now have two recommendations.*NEW RECOMMENDATIONDeere and Co=
. (DE) February 305 calls-- Symbol: DE210205C00305000-- Order: Buy at $3.70=
 lmt day only-- If filled, set up to sell half at $4.80 lmt gtc and half at=
 $6.30 lmt gtc-- If filled, set stop at $2.60 stp, good after 10:30 a.m. ET=
 only*Jon D. MarkmanAll recommendations are for monthly options expiring on=
 the third Friday of the specified month unless otherwise noted. All stops =
are good after 10:30 a.m. Eastern only unless otherwise specified. All orde=
rs are good for the day only unless otherwise noted. "Day only" orders expi=
re at the close of the current session. Past results are no guarantee of fu=
ture returns. All accounts may not achieve comparable results. Recommendati=
ons are leveraged and speculative, so only use risk capital =E2=80=94 i.e.,=
 money you can afford to lose. All results are shown ex-commissions and fee=
s. Options trading involves the risk of substantial loss. Some news and res=
earch provided by Wall Street Journal, Bloomberg, Associated Press, MT News=
wires and Reuters.&nbsp;

